# Secrets And Change Discipline

- Never commit `.env`, provider keys, databases, or local logs.
- Provider keys are memory-only and must never appear in commits, logs, or prompts.
- Hosted-provider tests use fixtures. Do not spend paid API credits without an explicit request.
- Make focused commits against `main`; never force-push shared branches.
- Migrations under `drizzle/` are append-only.
- Update `AGENTS.md` and `README.md` when commands, architecture, or deployment steps change.
